course: dictionary
lesson: 6272
title: Mongoose: a word with a plural
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A mongoose is a small, fast, furry animal with a long body and tail. The context tells you more: «The fossa is Madagascar's biggest meat-eater, shaped like a slim cat but related to mongooses.» Related to mongooses means the fossa is a relative of the mongoose, not a mongoose itself.
explain: Clues can also show what a word does. «In Kenya, hornbills and dwarf mongooses team up: the birds catch insects the mongooses disturb and call out warnings of hawks.» Team up means work together, so the birds and mongooses share a job.
explain: Check the plural too. «Mongoose comes from Marathi, a language of India, so its plural is mongooses.» Plural means more than one. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your idea in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: A mongoose is a small, fast, furry animal with a long body and tail.
fact: Mongooses come from Africa and Asia.
fact: Mongooses are famous for fighting and killing snakes, including cobras.
fact: In Rudyard Kipling's «The Jungle Book», Rikki-Tikki-Tavi is a brave mongoose who protects a family from cobras.
fact: The plural of «mongoose» is «mongooses», and a group of them is «a band of mongooses».
exercise: What is a mongoose? | A type of fish from the sea | *A small, fast, furry animal with a long body and tail | A large bird that lives in trees
exercise: Which word is the correct plural of mongoose? | mongoose-es | mongeese | *mongooses | mongooseys
exercise: In Kipling's story, what does Rikki-Tikki-Tavi protect a family from? | Hawks | Floods | Rain and wind | *Cobras
test: What do the hornbills and dwarf mongooses do together in Kenya? | They sleep in the same tree | *They work together, the birds catching insects the mongooses disturb | They hunt each other for food | They race each other across the savanna
test: Where do mongooses come from? | North America only | Antarctica | *Africa and Asia | Europe only
exam: When mongooses were brought to islands like Hawaii to kill rats, what else happened? | They turned into rats | They left the islands and went home | *They also killed native birds | They became friends with the birds
